-- Names come from research/re/pt_symbols.txt (`arm-none-eabi-nm -n` over the matching build), but a
-- symbol is only a lead. ⭐ EVERY VALUE BELOW WAS READ BACK OUT OF OLA'S OWN CARTRIDGE at the point
-- of use, by both engineers independently on 2026-09-04 — Claude with capstone, Codex with the new
-- research/re/pt_dis.py, full evidence in team/report-20260904-pt-dialogue-anchors.md. Nothing here
-- rests on a C struct definition (Rule 5).
--
-- ⚠ A THUMB FUNCTION POINTER IS STORED WITH BIT 0 SET. nm prints the even address; the value the
-- game writes into a callback field is that address + 1. Identity comparisons below use the STORED
-- form, and getting this wrong would make every gate silently fail closed forever. Proof that this
-- is not theory: the EVEN words 0x0203cccc and 0x0203e950 appear ZERO times in the whole ARM9
-- image, while the odd ones appear in the templates and literal pools that install them.
