-- 3b) MYSTERY GIFT AND THE WONDER CARD ALBUM — two applications in the main-menu overlay (97).
--
-- ⭐ BOTH ARE TOP-LEVEL APPLICATIONS, and each hands over to the other by enqueueing it:
-- MysteryGiftApp_Exit enqueues the album when CHECK CARD was chosen (0x022301DE-0x022301E2, pool
-- {0x61, 0x0223D7AC}), and WonderCardsApp_Exit enqueues Mystery Gift again on the way out
-- (0x02231FC4-0x02231FC8, pool {0x61, 0x0223D71C}). So sApplication +0x04 names whichever one is up
-- and the main-menu module, which matches MainMenu_Main, can never claim either (Rule 2). Both
-- templates say FS_OVERLAY_ID_NONE, so the overlay is checked where the enqueue parked it,
-- sApplication +0x00 — the same 0xFFFFFFFF trap the main menu itself has.
--   ApplicationManager +0x14 procState: the app's own state machine (ApplicationManager_Exec passes
--   `adds r1,#0x14`). MysteryGiftApp_Main 0x0222F77C `ldr r3,[r5]; cmp r3,#0x39` switches on it over
--   58 states; WonderCardsApp_Main 0x02231628 `ldr r1,[r5]; cmp r1,#0x1d` over 30.
--
-- ⛔ ALMOST NOTHING HERE IS LIVE TEXT, AND THE ONE THING THAT IS NEEDS NO BAKING. Every message,
-- label and value both apps draw is expanded into a String, rasterized and FREED in the same call
-- (ShowMessageBox frees at 0x0222DEE2; DetermineGiftStatus at 0x0223096C; PrintTextEntryToWindow,
-- ShowWindowsForScreen and ShowWindowFromTemplateIndex the same way), so those words are baked from
-- the cartridge by research/re/gen_pt_mystery_gift_text.py and the VALUES are read from the data the
-- game formats them from. The exceptions are read live:
--   * MENU ROWS. MakeStateChangeListMenuFromEntryTemplates keeps the StringList until the NEXT menu
--     is built (it frees the old one first, 0x0222DD2E / 0x02230536), so a row's own String is
--     on the heap for as long as its menu is the one taking input.
--   * THE PAGED MESSAGES. ShowMessageBoxIntoStateTransition parks its String at appData +0x14
--     (0x0222E262) and frees it only once the printer has finished (0x0222E292), and the app sits
