	local GENDER = 0x84                    -- playerGender. ⚠ ROM-derived like everything else here:
	                                       -- RowanIntro_DisplayMessage 0x021D1594 reaches it as
	                                       -- `adds r3,r5,#0; adds r3,#0x84; ldr r3,[r3]` on its way
	                                       -- into StringTemplate_SetString, alongside +0x70
	                                       -- playerNamingScreenArgs and +0x74 the rival's.

	-- ⛔ THE INFO SCREENS ("view controls", "about your adventure") ARE BAKED, AND THEY HAVE TO BE.
	-- This is the one place in the Platinum file that does not read live text, and the reason is a
	-- lifetime, not laziness: RowanIntro_DisplayTextBlock creates its String, loads the message,
	-- renders it INSTANTLY and calls String_Free — all inside DTB_STATE_INIT, one call, one frame
	-- (the free is the `bl 0x20237bc` at 0x021D18A6). By the time the screen is up and being read,
	-- the text is gone. There is NO frame on which a reader could see it alive, and reading it dead
	-- is the use-after-free class this project has been burned by twice.
	--
	-- ⚠ THIS IS WHY "view controls" WAS SILENT (Ola, 2026-09-05). My gate asked for
	-- displayTextBlockState 1..4 — every one of which is AFTER the free — so the reader was looking
	-- at a poisoned String and correctly refusing it. Fixed by baking, keyed on the scene state,
	-- which is what says which screen is up.
	--
