			-- is pressed inside a circle of radius 16 centred on (128, 100) —
			-- RowanIntro_WasPokeballOpened tests exactly `dx*dx + dy*dy <= 16*16` about that point —
			-- and a button press does nothing except trigger the "touch the button" message, which
			-- then returns here. That is the loop Ola hit: "it kept speaking the same message over
			-- and over again when I pressed a button." It was the game working as designed, and
			-- there was no way past it without a finger.
			--
			-- ⛔ SO IT IS THE SAME CHORD AS BLACK AND WHITE, NOT A RULE OF ITS OWN (Ola, 2026-09-05:
			-- "any button shouldn't tap it, we have a touch layer which we use on black and white
			-- with specific keys for how to use it, we can't change behaviour here"). HOLD THE RIGHT
			-- TRIGGER AND PRESS CONFIRM — the "H" the Musical and the fly map already use. A screen
			-- that needs the touch screen is registered with core/pad.lua and driven by the chords
			-- Ola already knows; inventing a per-screen shortcut would make the layer meaningless.
			if scene == ST_PKBL_WAIT_INPUT and pressed["H"] and not touch.busy() then
				touch.tap(128, 100, 6)
			end

