	--
	-- Ola, 2026-09-06: "for black and white we have the npcs as clurke, man, or something that we
	-- found... I don't really want to go out of the town until we have something working."
	--
	-- ⭐ BLACK AND WHITE'S ANSWER IS ITS `MODEL_NPC` TABLE, and it is worth being precise about which
	-- layer that is, because I had it wrong until I went and read the file. Its naming chain ends
	-- `... story name -> role -> vendor -> zone name -> MODEL_NPC[sprite] -> "Person"`, so the SPRITE
	-- is the catch-all that sits last and is the reason almost nobody there reads as "Person". The
	-- speaker-prefix trick everyone remembers is the layer ABOVE it and only names story characters.
	--
	-- This is the same layer for Platinum, generated by research/re/gen_pt_npc_names.py, and the
	-- cartridge supplies most of it through two routes that were checked against each other over
	-- every object in the game and disagreed nowhere:
	--   * the sprite's own name matched to a LOCALIZED trainer class — the decompilation names every
	--     sprite (`OBJ_EVENT_GFX_*`) and those names are never spoken, they only choose which of the
	--     game's own words applies. Same "names propose, cartridge disposes" split as the buildings.
	--   * the one class a sight trainer wears it as, where the first is silent.
	-- **896 of the 1,569 people who read "Person" get one of the GAME'S words.** A further 394 get one
	-- of OURS — a cashier, a nurse, a gym guide, an old man — because Platinum has no trainer class
	-- for those roles and no word for them anywhere, which is the same allowed exception Black and
	-- White made and the same one "House" already is here.
	--
	-- ⛔ WHO THIS TABLE DELIBERATELY DOES NOT NAME, and where they are named instead. The gym
	-- leaders, Cynthia, Looker, Mom and the Galactic admins all have REAL names in the cartridge, so
	-- emitting a decompiler's constant here would be inventing English where the game has the thing
	-- itself. They are named by STORY_SPRITE and STORY_SCRIPT below, from the game's own words.
	-- The rival and the counterpart are named from the SAVE, because their names were never in any
	-- table: one the player typed, the other decided by the player's gender.
	-- Overworld Pokémon are named by STORY_SCRIPT too, in the cartridge's own capitals — "PIKACHU",
	-- not "Pikachu" (Ola, questions_open.md round 2 Q2 = A: the game's text, not ours).
	-- ⭐ TEAM GALACTIC'S GRUNTS STAY WITH THIS TABLE ON HIS INSTRUCTION (round 2 Q1 = C). Their own
	-- dialogue calls them "Grunt 1" and "Grunt 2", which are SCENE labels that swap round from room
	-- to room, so those words are excluded from the script bake and the sprite answers instead.
	-- ⚠ What it actually says is "Galactic" — the cartridge's own trainer-class word — not "Team
	-- Galactic", which is ours and belongs to the three- and four-grunt group sprites. He chose C
	-- believing it said the latter; flagged to him rather than silently changed.
